 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sukkah.37a.5",
   "daf": "37a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "רַבִּי מֵאִיר אוֹמֵר אֲפִילּוּ בִּמְשִׁיחָה כּוּ׳. תַּנְיָא אָמַר רַבִּי מֵאִיר: מַעֲשֶׂה בְּיַקִּירֵי יְרוּשָׁלַיִם שֶׁהָיוּ אוֹגְדִין אֶת לוּלְבֵיהֶן בְּגִימוֹנִיּוֹת שֶׁל זָהָב. אָמְרוּ לוֹ: מִשָּׁם רְאָיָה?! בְּמִינוֹ הָיוּ אוֹגְדִין אוֹתוֹ מִלְּמַטָּה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues: «Rabbi Meir says:» One may tie the lulav «even with a cord. It is taught» in the Tosefta that «Rabbi Meir said:» There was «an incident involving the prominent» residents «of Jerusalem who would bind their lulavim with gold rings.» The Sages «said to him:» Is there «proof from there? They would bind it with its own species beneath» the rings, which serve a merely decorative purpose and not a halakhic one."
  }
 ],
